 ## Subtopics
 
+### [NDC Points to Distance](2500-ndc-points-to-distance.md)
+Converts sampled Normalized Device Coordinates (NDC) points to segment distances between consecutive samples along a ray, accounting for the cosine of the viewing angle. It operates directly in NDC space, where uniform sampling steps do not correspond to uniform physical distances, unlike linear depth-to-distance methods. Choose this when rendering with NDC sampling schemes rather than linear depth sampling.
